what is Java:

Platform independent Language
WORA( write once Run Anywhere)


working: 

JAVA FILE ---- compiler ---- .class file [ Bytecode ] ----- JVM ---- machine code ---- CPU ---- output

The compiler is 
  - JIT Compiler

  
  
3 Main Components:

JDK ( JRE ( JVM ) JRE ) JDK

JVM :
- Java Virtual Machine
  - It's an abstract machine(doesn;t exist physically)
  - this is platform dependent
  - for diff os it needs to have compatible jvm

JRE:
- Java RunTime Environment
  - It has JVM  + 
  - class libraries
  - with JRE you can run any file

  with only jre you can't code 
  and compile
  
JDK
- Java Development Kit
  - programming language
  - compiler( javac)
  - debugger
  
